<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=punched-card">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Communication and computing</p><h1 class="enc-title">Punched card</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1725">1725</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Punch card, Hollerith card, IBM card</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A punched card is a stiff paper medium that stores information by the presence or absence of holes in fixed positions. Basile Bouchon controlled a loom by punched holes in paper tape in 1725, and his assistant Jean-Baptiste Falcon and Jacques Vaucanson improved the design. In 1804 Joseph Marie Jacquard linked multiple punched cards into a chain of any length to automate loom operation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herman-hollerith">Herman Hollerith</a> developed punched-card data processing for the 1890 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a>. The IBM 12-row, 80-column format came to dominate, and cards remained in use for data and programs until the mid-1980s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/punched-card.jpg" alt="Punched card" width="330" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Antonio González Nieto - cropped by Eyesinthefire · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2punchCards-square.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1725</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Basile Bouchon · <a href="/encyclopedia/herman-hollerith">Herman Hollerith</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Bouchon's 1725 control used punched paper tape, not cards; chained cards date from Jacquard in 1804. Punched holes for control and storage were devised independently several times, among them Semyon Korsakov, who announced punched cards for storing and searching information in September 1832.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/loom">Loom<span>c. 4400 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/jacquard-machine">Jacquard machine<span>1804</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=punched-card">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
